From: PikuZheng <cba321123@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:45:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(server): make connection close idempotent via atomic closed guard
Origin: https://github.com/PikuZheng/smartdns/commit/beb498142d131501e2d4ecd6a0318c4ccf846d34
Upstream-Status: Backported from downstream PikuZheng/canary

_dns_server_client_close is called from 9 different sites and was non-idempotent.
Concurrent or overlapping close invocations caused over-release of refcnt,
prematurely freeing conn and triggering fatal Use-After-Free crashes.
Add an atomic_t closed guard to ensure only the first closer performs teardown.
---
diff --git a/src/dns_server/connection.c b/src/dns_server/connection.c
index 63dc1f94..694522cd 100644
--- a/src/dns_server/connection.c
+++ b/src/dns_server/connection.c
@@ -164,6 +164,11 @@ void _dns_server_client_touch(struct dns_server_conn_head *conn)
 
 int _dns_server_client_close(struct dns_server_conn_head *conn)
 {
+	/* Only the first closer tears the connection down; later calls must not drop another refcnt. */
+	if (atomic_inc_return(&conn->closed) != 1) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (conn->fd > 0) {
 		_dns_server_epoll_ctl(conn, EPOLL_CTL_DEL, 0);
 	}
diff --git a/src/dns_server/dns_server.h b/src/dns_server/dns_server.h
index 902eebff..8827dadc 100644
--- a/src/dns_server/dns_server.h
+++ b/src/dns_server/dns_server.h
@@ -143,6 +143,7 @@ struct dns_server_conn_head {
 	struct list_head list;
 	time_t last_request_time;
 	atomic_t refcnt;
+	atomic_t closed;
 	const char *dns_group;
 	uint32_t server_flags;
 	struct nftset_ipset_rules *ipset_nftset_rule;
-- 
